Step 11.5 is implemented and verified. Summary:

**New provider blueprint** — `studio/providers/` (`routes.py` + `catalog.py`), registered in `app.py`. Thirteen handlers, all loopback-only and all using the `{"error": {"code","message","details?"}}` envelope:

| surface | endpoints |
|---|---|
| catalog | `GET /api/providers` → `{catalog_version, domains}`, `GET /api/providers/<domain>` |
| detail | `GET /api/providers/<d>/<p>`, `.../capabilities` |
| health | `GET .../health` (stored settings), `POST .../test` (candidate patch) |
| settings | `GET/PUT .../settings`, `POST .../validate` |
| selection | `PUT /api/providers/<domain>/selection` (new, D13) |
| document | `GET/PUT/PATCH /api/settings/v2` (`PATCH` new, D13) |

`studio/editor/routes.py` lost 189 lines and no longer imports `settings_manager`; the URLs are unchanged, so no consumer broke.

**Defect found and fixed:** `_rebind_new_runtimes` re-ran `register_runtime()` for every provider on each catalog reload — a second claim on an already-registered `@sock.route`. The hub now keeps a `(domain, provider_id)` binding ledger, cleared on `shutdown()`.

**Frontend:** `useProviders.selectProvider` replaced its `GET → spread → PUT /api/settings/v2` read-modify-write (a real lost-update window plus a redundant validate round trip) with the one targeted call. No Vue component changed.

**Adjustments recorded in the plan** — the "deprecated facade" is a no-op because the paths didn't move; "deprecated" providers are enumerated via `aliases` since §20.1 declares no such flag; the API became loopback-only (it wasn't); and `PUT /api/settings/v2` stays permissive so whole-document import still works.

Verification: 545 backend tests (10 live skipped, 198 subtests), 160 frontend tests / 26 files, Vite build, docs drift — all green. Both new guards were mutation-checked.

